  "notes": [
    "Historical fixtures predate per-feed attribution, so the replay cannot reproduce a specific feed's price; live legs still require attribution.",
    "Replay prices come from one stored bookmaker trio per fixture, so the result is conservative and does not assume access to every book.",
    "Settlement uses the stored final score. Each combo is staked flat and returns stake \u00d7 total odds only when every leg wins.",
    "One ticket per size per matchday is settled: the engine's top-ranked combo. Evaluating several overlapping tickets per day would count the same legs more than once.",
    "Combined probability is the product of de-vigged market probabilities, which assumes the legs are independent. Near-duplicate fixtures are collapsed to one leg before combinations are built.",
    "The latest 30% of matchdays is the holdout; the fit is validated on its most recent slice and stored only when it reduces held-out log loss.",
    "The after-learning holdout re-selects legs with a calibration fitted on training matchdays only, so that comparison stays out of sample.",
    "At a bookmaker's own prices, a negative ROI is expected: the margin is already inside the price. Hit rate above the required break-even is the measure of whether the tier is worth playing.",
    "A calibration fitted on training matchdays only did not clear its own held-out improvement bar (0.00031 < 0.002), so no after-learning holdout comparison is published."
